# ea2468 example sets exceed GitHub's 100 MB per-file push limit
# (rs_1n ~96 MB, rs_2n ~193 MB, rs_3n ~290 MB; this repo has no git-lfs).
# Transferred out of band, deposited on Zenodo at publication — same treatment
# as the ea2468 bias above. Decided 2026-08-21.
/data/examples/ea2468_rs_1n.json
/data/examples/ea2468_rs_2n.json
/data/examples/ea2468_rs_3n.json
/tests/output/
/.serena/

# SoSyM sweep: partials are the only genuine intermediate. Gate 0 proved the merged
# CV JSON reconstructs them exactly, so they are regenerable and ignored.
#
# EXCEPTION, and the reason the rule needs one: that reconstruction argument holds
# only for a unit whose folds are ALL done. While a unit is part-finished there is no
# merged file, so its partials are the only copy of that compute. Force-add those
# (git add -f) until the unit completes and the merged file supersedes them.
#
# The generated configs are NOT intermediates and are tracked. They carry the
# provenance of every run — seed, shuffle_bias, solver_mode, n_folds, max_queries,
# query_mode and the exact input paths. At 0b0313a the committed config said
# query_mode = "example_only" while the commit shipped example-first results from an
# uncommitted edit, and those numbers cannot be reproduced as a result. shuffle_bias
# is load-bearing besides: ADR-0015's defect bites precisely when the pool seed is
# None, which is precisely when that flag is false.
data/results_sosym/**/partials/

# Scratch output from re-running a single cell. The worked example in the README writes
# here, so a reader who follows it does not end up with an untracked directory and a
# tree that looks modified when nothing is wrong.
scratch/
